  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef has 222 numbers AAA and BBB (A&lt;B)(A \\lt B)(A&lt;B).\n\nChef will perform some operations on AAA.\n\nIn the ithi^{th}ith operation:\n\n\nChef will add 111 to AAA if iii is odd.\nChef will add 222 to AAA if iii is even.\nChef can stop at any instant. Can Chef make AAA equal to BBB?\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains a single integer TTT — the number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\nThe first and only line of each test case contains two space separated integers AAA and BBB.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output `YES` if Chef can make AAA and BBB equal, `NO` otherwise.\n\n\nNote that the checker is case-insensitive. So, `YES`, `Yes`, `yEs` are all considered same.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤10001 \\leq T \\leq 10001≤T≤1000",
      "1≤A&lt;B≤1091 \\leq A \\lt B \\leq 10^91≤A&lt;B≤109"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n1 2\n3 6\n4 9\n10 20",
        "output": "YES\nYES\nNO\nYES",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 1: Chef may perform one operation to make AAA equal to BBB: 1→+121 \\xrightarrow{+1} 21+1​2\nTest case 2: 3→+14→+263 \\xrightarrow{+1} 4 \\xrightarrow{+2} 63+1​4+2​6\nTest case 3: It can be shown that it is impossible to make AAA and BBB equal.\nTest case 4: 10→+111→+213→+114→+216→+117→+219→+12010 \\xrightarrow{+1} 11 \\xrightarrow{+2} 13 \\xrightarrow{+1} 14 \\xrightarrow{+2} 16 \\xrightarrow{+1} 17 \\xrightarrow{+2} 19 \\xrightarrow{+1} 2010+1​11+2​13+1​14+2​16+1​17+2​19+1​20"
      }
    ]
  },
